atched cottage, overwhelmed with grief and bathed in tears.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.681,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-46-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3044011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"25b03917c228e3bc5d775daf22d2ebd13eae52a74a203025d082a036e70f73b9","compact":"21986d98aad0967fb3e5b29d1b17d806ce35309fe80efafe4c6fa437b1d58f0e","nasal":"039611cf78e2ec9b7d7e388bf229f44c12b10db895f9caba3e9addd78090e5c6"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-44-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":44,"verse":12,"english":"And that ranger of the night with a pleased heart approached Vaidehī.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.712,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-46-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3044012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7ade19f77d92a90b7dae37da316099da857136cc9b391460b493763a2f82c47e","compact":"8aaecb865fcaecb614898f848b312116739b441137221731180b4e5c214858f4","nasal":"8aaecb865fcaecb614898f848b312116739b441137221731180b4e5c214858f4"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-44-13","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":44,"verse":13,"english":"Seeing her that lord of Rākṣasas was pierced with the shafts of passion. And speaking highly of her, surpassing in beauty the three worlds and resembling by the excellence of her own person the very goddess of wealth herself Rāvana uttering the name of God spake to her,","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.703,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-46-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3044013","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"542307afe3caaefa1f5091652c406e9f27160978bc7ceb8053fcd0885f4e5faa","compact":"238000a41265cef0a3ad570ec319640475a6e304d4020857389df5c228da0b02","nasal":"238000a41265cef0a3ad570ec319640475